        },
        {
          "id": "the_link_is_interpolated_between_its_two_brackets",
          "description": "FACES THE REFERENCE. The link's 30 mi/h sits between schedule 1021 at 20.6006 and schedule 153 at 30.5, so the factor is 9.3994/9.8994 = 0.9494918883972766 and the link is 95 % of the way to the faster cycle. The snapshot stores mode 1000 at `1.12522e-01` and mode 1011 at `9.00282e-02`; the assertions are at `rel 1e-6` because that is the reference's own FLOAT-column rendering and not a port tolerance -- the whole-corpus residual is 2.396e-06 and every one of the 122 cells is exact at six digits (docs/link-operating-mode-distribution.md 7.1). Mode 1030 is asserted because the LOW bracket never enters it: the interpolation runs over the full physics mode band with `coalesce(missing, 0)` and drops non-positives afterwards, so a mode only one bracket reached still appears. Running the union of the two brackets' modes instead loses 6 cells in the oracle.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "lomd_interpolationFactor",
              "time": 0.0,
